    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 49,
        "line": 2,
        "text": "America was God’s light on this earth, America was the world’s good Samaritan. But along the way we lost our strength, and our world is fallen. We forgot our place in God’s plan for America."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 5,
        "line": 859,
        "text": "Coming up on this wall of a sudden and seeing how black it was, it was so awful, but then I came down in it and saw that white carnation sticking out of that crack, and it gave me hope. It made me know He’s watching over us."
      }
